### Anything else?

Suggested fix — delete the bucket only if the map still holds it:

```ts
bucket.idleId = null;

if (bucket.queue.size > 0) {
  this.scheduleBucket(bucket, options);
} else if (this.buckets.get(key) === bucket) {
  this.buckets.delete(key);
}
```

Workaround in tests: `deferBlockBehavior: DeferBlockBehavior.Manual` for specs that render such a tree, so that no idle trigger is scheduled at all.

